Negative control for the mocking treatment's geometry (`R6-18`).

Swaps the outline for a border, a padding and a background fill — the SAME
primary family, the same chip, the same armed-only condition — so the colour
claim (`H2`) still passes and the only thing that can go red is the ruled one:
mocking must not change the page's geometry. A border and a padding reserve
space, so every column under the frame moves the moment a preset arms or a track
plays, and the fill repaints the page underneath; an outline reserves none,
which is why it is the technique the row-error ring already uses (`H10`).

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the forced-canvas geometry case — the armed frame adds no border, no
padding and no background, and the page's own box is what it was on Live.

